{"ref":"BDB, מַבָּט²","hw":"מַבָּט²","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">מַבָּט</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:5\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.5\">Zc 9:5</a></sup> <strong>expectation</strong> = object of hope or confidence <strong>(</strong>lit. <em>thing looked to</em><strong>)</strong>;—sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַבָּטֵנוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 20:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.20.6\">Is 20:6</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מַבָּטָס</span> v <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 20:5\" href=\"/Isaiah.20.5\">5</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מֶבָּטָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:5\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.5\">Zc 9:5</a>;—of Cush as ally of Judah <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 20:5\" href=\"/Isaiah.20.5\">Is 20:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 20:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.20.6\">6</a>; of Tyre as ally of Philistia <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:5\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.5\">Zc 9:5</a>.","next":"BDB, נְבָט","prev":"BDB, נָבַט"}